.TH webhttrack 1 "07 October 2026" "httrack website copier"
.SH NAME
webhttrack \- offline browser : copy websites to a local directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B webhttrack [browse] [htsserver option value ..] [key value ..]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B webhttrack
starts the
.BR htsserver (1)
web server and opens the WebHTTrack interface in a browser. The interface drives the
.BR httrack (1)
engine to copy websites to a local directory, by default
.IR ~/websites .
The server stops once the interface is closed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B browse
open the mirrored projects (~/websites/index.html) instead
.TP
.B \-\-port <port>
passed to htsserver (default: the first free port from 8080)
.TP
.B \-\-bind <address>
passed to htsserver (default: 127.0.0.1)
.TP
.B \-\-ping\-timeout <secs>
passed to htsserver
.TP
.B key value
any other pair is passed to htsserver
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
print this help and exit
.TP
.B \-\-version
print the version and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B webhttrack
open the interface
.TP
.B webhttrack browse
open the mirrored projects without starting the interface
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IP BROWSER
The browser to open, through xdg\-open or sensible\-browser. Without it,
.B webhttrack
tries a list of known browsers.
.IP "LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES, LANG"
The first one set picks the language of the interface, until the interface saves its own choice in
.IR ~/.httrack.ini .
.IP HOME
Projects are kept in
.I ~/websites
unless the interface is told otherwise.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.httrack.ini
.RS
The interface settings. Its
.I path=
line names the projects directory that
.I browse
opens.
.RE
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Each mirror writes its errors and warnings to
.I hts\-log.txt
in the project directory.
.SH BUGS
